p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="139" name="Google Shape;139;p14"/><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr><p:ph idx="1" type="body"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="819150" y="1990725"/><a:ext cx="7505700" cy="2448000"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr anchorCtr="0" anchor="t" bIns="91425" lIns="91425" spcFirstLastPara="1" rIns="91425" wrap="square" tIns="91425"><a:noAutofit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr indent="457200" lvl="0" marL="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en"/><a:t>What is matter? Matter is basically any material or </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en"/><a:t>substance</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en"/><a:t> that contains mass and volume. It is everywhere and includes substances such as water, the atmosphere, you, your chair etc. </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en"/><a:t>Matter is made up of atoms and in those atoms there are little particles called protons, neutrons, and electrons. The protons and neutrons are at the center of the atom while the electrons rotate around them. </a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" lvl="0" marL="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="1600"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="1600"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en"/><a:t>	Matter also can be in properties. Properties are a way to classify matter. There are two types of properties: Physical and Chemical. Physical properties are properties in matter that you can physically see. Describing a sponge: yellow, not dense, and is able to absorb. Those are all Physical properties. Now chemical properties are very similar to physical properties except it has to do with the chemical makeup of the substance. For example cake has a chemical property where it when it reacts to an oven (intense heat) it rises up and hardens. </a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr id="140" name="Google Shape;140;p14"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="5860038" y="220075"/><a:ext cx="3076575" cy="1485900"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr id="141" name="Google Shape;141;p14"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId4"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="3719248" y="220075"/><a:ext cx="2140800" cy="1603525"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr><mc:AlternateContent><mc:Choice Requires="p14"><p:transition spd="slow" p14:dur="4400"><p:push dir="r"/></p:transition></mc:Choice><mc:Fallback><p:transition spd="slow"><p:fade/></p:transition></mc:Fallback></mc:AlternateContent></p:sld>